{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction to the plan's Context section, recorded after the plan-review E4 advisory (which was right) and fixed in the commit message on patchset 2 of Gerrit 1916.\n\nThe plan said 'every mutation primitive in git_adapter.py carries a function-level # raw-git-ok: marker'. Only FOUR do: rm_cached (git_adapter.py:184), update_ref (:230), add (:246), commit (:252). read_tree, write_tree and commit_tree carry none — and the reason is itself evidence for R3: R1/R2 only fire on verbs in MUTATION_VERBS ({add, commit, rm, mv, reset, update-ref, checkout, clean}), and 'read-tree'/'write-tree'/'commit-tree' are NOT in that set. Those three primitives were therefore invisible to the pre-R3 gate entirely, not merely sanctioned by it. That widens the original archaeology rather than narrowing it: __main__.py's detached-index purge composed five primitives, THREE of which no rule could ever have seen.\n\nThe description text is left as-is deliberately — editing it now would invalidate the signed plan-review attestation for a wording fix; the accurate statement lives here and in the landed commit message."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787174716333926001,"uuid":"14018ec2-148c-428b-9329-4fad297b087d"}